\description{
Collects the cross-dataset information \code{\link[=summary.admiral_df]{summary.admiral_df()}} reports when a
subject-level dataset is supplied via its \code{adsl} argument. ADSL is the
subject-level source of truth -- the full subject universe, the
authoritative treatment/population values, and the subject-level events
a record-level dataset must respect -- so a dataset can be wrong \emph{relative to
ADSL} in ways it can never reveal on its own: subjects with no ADSL entry,
